Using Grafana for Kubernetes Monitoring
Lab Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

Install and configure a local Kubernetes cluster using Minikube
Deploy Prometheus monitoring system in Kubernetes
Install and configure Grafana for data visualization
Integrate Prometheus as a data source in Grafana
Create comprehensive dashboards for monitoring Kubernetes cluster health
Monitor key Kubernetes metrics including node health, pod status, and resource utilization
Understand the relationship between Prometheus metrics collection and Grafana visualization
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

Basic understanding of Linux command line operations
Familiarity with containerization concepts (Docker)
Basic knowledge of Kubernetes concepts (pods, services, deployments)
Understanding of monitoring and observability principles
Experience with YAML configuration files
