Task 3: Create Dashboards for Kubernetes Metrics
Subtask 3.1: Import Pre-built Kubernetes Dashboard
Step 1: Import Kubernetes cluster monitoring dashboard

Click on + (plus icon) in the left sidebar
Select Import
Enter dashboard ID: 3119 (Kubernetes cluster monitoring dashboard)
Click Load
Select Prometheus as the data source
Click Import
Step 2: Explore the imported dashboard

The dashboard will display various Kubernetes metrics including:

Cluster CPU usage
Memory utilization
Pod status
Node information
Network traffic
Subtask 3.2: Create Custom Dashboard for Pod Monitoring
Step 1: Create a new dashboard

Click on + (plus icon) in the left sidebar
Select Dashboard
Click Add new panel
Step 2: Configure CPU usage panel

In the query editor, enter the following PromQL query:
sum(rate(container_cpu_usage_seconds_total{container!="POD",container!=""}[5m])) by (pod)
Set Panel Title: "Pod CPU Usage"
Set Unit: "percent (0-100)"
Click Apply
Step 3: Add Memory usage panel

Click Add panel
Enter the following query:
sum(container_memory_usage_bytes{container!="POD",container!=""}) by (pod) / 1024 / 1024
Set Panel Title: "Pod Memory Usage (MB)"
Set Unit: "bytes"
Click Apply
Step 4: Add Pod status panel

Click Add panel
Enter the following query:
kube_pod_status_phase
Set Panel Title: "Pod Status"
Change visualization type to Stat
Click Apply
Step 5: Save the dashboard

Click the Save icon (disk icon) at the top
Enter Dashboard name: "Custom Kubernetes Pod Monitoring"
Click Save
Subtask 3.3: Create Node Monitoring Dashboard
Step 1: Create another new dashboard

Click on + (plus icon) in the left sidebar
Select Dashboard
Click Add new panel
Step 2: Configure Node CPU panel

Enter the following query:
100 - (avg by (instance) (rate(node_cpu_seconds_total{mode="idle"}[5m])) * 100)
Set Panel Title: "Node CPU Usage (%)"
Set Unit: "percent (0-100)"
Click Apply
Step 3: Add Node Memory panel

Click Add panel
Enter the following query:
(1 - (node_memory_MemAvailable_bytes / node_memory_MemTotal_bytes)) * 100
Set Panel Title: "Node Memory Usage (%)"
Set Unit: "percent (0-100)"
Click Apply
Step 4: Add Disk usage panel

Click Add panel
Enter the following query:
100 - ((node_filesystem_avail_bytes{mountpoint="/",fstype!="rootfs"} / node_filesystem_size_bytes{mountpoint="/",fstype!="rootfs"}) * 100)
Set Panel Title: "Node Disk Usage (%)"
Set Unit: "percent (0-100)"
Click Apply
Step 5: Save the node dashboard

Click the Save icon
Enter Dashboard name: "Kubernetes Node Monitoring"
Click Save
